From: Medvedolog <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] unisocwifi: derive SoftAP beacon channel from cfg80211 chandef

OpenWrt/hostapd passes the selected AP channel in settings->chandef. The
vendor driver ignored it and only rewrote beacon channel IEs when a debug
softap_channel or STA+SoftAP SCC channel happened to be configured.

That leaves userspace reporting channel 36 / AP-ENABLED while firmware
receives an unadjusted START_AP beacon and no 5 GHz SSID is emitted.

Use the cfg80211 primary channel as the normal input to the existing vendor
beacon rewrite path. Keep STA+SoftAP SCC and debug softap_channel as higher
priority overrides.

Do not issue WIFI_CMD_SET_CHANNEL here. Hardware testing showed that sending
that command before START_AP asserts rf_marlin and resets WCN on UWE5622.

---
diff --git a/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c b/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
--- a/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
+++ b/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
@@ -979,6 +979,13 @@ static int sprdwl_cfg80211_start_ap(struct wiphy *wiphy,
 #endif
 	vif->ssid_len = settings->ssid_len;
 
+	/* START_AP derives the RF channel from the beacon. Feed the channel
+	 * selected by cfg80211 into the vendor beacon rewrite path instead of
+	 * issuing WIFI_CMD_SET_CHANNEL, which crashes this firmware.
+	 */
+	if (settings->chandef.chan)
+		chn = settings->chandef.chan->hw_value;
+
 #ifdef STA_SOFTAP_SCC_MODE
 	chn = intf->sta_home_channel;
 #endif
